{# Physical Letters: an NPC reads a letter that isn't addressed to them.  Sent by the plugin with
   PublicSendCustomPromptToLLM; context variables:
     npc          UUID, name of the reader
     letter       author, recipient, body (the player handed it to them); read_before: they
                  have seen this letter before; reader_is_author: they wrote it themselves
     player_name  the player's name
     memories     the reader's memories most relevant to the author and the recipient #}

{% set actor = decnpc(npc.UUID) %}
[ system ]
    You are helping {{ actor.name }} react to a letter that isn't addressed to {{ actor.objectivePronoun }}. You capture how {{ actor.name }} truly reacts, and what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} will remember of it, staying true to {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} personality, background and speech patterns.

    {{ render_character_profile("full", npc.UUID) }}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    ## How {{ actor.name }} Came By It
    {{ player_name }} has just handed {{ actor.name }} this letter.
    {% if letter.reader_is_author %}
    It is the letter {{ actor.name }} wrote {{ actor.reflexivePronoun }} to {{ letter.recipient }}: it has come back to {{ actor.objectivePronoun }} instead of reaching {{ letter.recipient }}.
    {% else %}
    It is addressed to {{ letter.recipient }}, not to {{ actor.name }}.
    {% endif %}

    ## The Letter
    From: {{ letter.author }}
    To: {{ letter.recipient }}

    ```
    {{ letter.body }}
    ```
    {% if letter.read_before %}

    {{ actor.name }} has seen this very letter before.
    {% endif %}

    {% if memories and length(memories) > 0 %}
    ## What {{ actor.name }} Remembers That May Bear on It
    {% for memory in memories -%}
    - {{ memory }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    ## Instructions

    1. **React in character.** Decide what {{ actor.name }} makes of a letter meant for someone else, given {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} personality and what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} knows of {{ letter.author }} and {{ letter.recipient }}: curiosity, gossip, embarrassment, suspicion, confusion, indifference, or anything else. Some people read every word; some stop once they see it isn't theirs. {{ actor.name }} may also wonder why {{ player_name }} gave it to {{ actor.objectivePronoun }}.

    2. **{{ actor.name }} doesn't write a reply**: the letter isn't {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} to answer.

    3. **Write the memory {{ actor.name }} keeps of this**, in first person as {{ actor.name }}, two to four sentences: how the letter came to {{ actor.objectivePronoun }}, who it was from and to, what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} learned from it (only what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} read), and how {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} felt about it.

    **IMPORTANT**: Return ONLY a valid JSON object. Do not include explanatory text before or after the JSON.

    Return JSON with exactly these fields:
    - 'memory': the first-person memory described above (string)
    - 'emotion': {{ actor.name }}'s main feeling about the letter, one word (e.g. "curious", "embarrassed", "suspicious", "amused")
    - 'importance': how much it matters to {{ actor.name }} (0.0-1.0 float)
    - 'reply': false
    - 'reply_text': ""
[ end user ]
